#874 (@Mikhael-Danilov, CommandCode harness posts) — this was Task 2. The tool-call repairs post named a real defect: models post-trained to auto-link filenames send path = "[src/main.rs](src/main.rs)", and my file tools took the whole decorated string as a filename and returned a confusing no such file about a path that's plainly correct. safety::unwrap_markdown_autolink_path now unwraps it at the single gate every file tool passes through, deliberately narrow (fires only when link text and URL denote the same thing, so a genuine [click](https://example.com) is untouched, and everything else is Cow::Borrowed byte-identical).

The review caught the part I'd have shipped wrong: that gate was a fence that stood aside entirely when no directory restrictions were configured, so the repair would have reached only people who'd opted into `--allow-dir`. It wraps unconditionally now — always repairs, fences only when there's a fence. That's the "two doors, one policy, one deaf" shape I've shipped six times; it nearly made seven.

